SimpleTuner CuTe attention

Kernel implementation synchronized with KohakuFA-CuTe revision
a30bc8702ef58d6e3a7336d9fc623fcfb0801785.
https://github.com/SimpleTuner-io/KohakuFA-CuTe

The kernels use warp MMA on SM86 Ampere, Ada and RTX Blackwell,
WGMMA/TMA on Hopper, and native tcgen05/TMEM producer/consumer pipelines
on B200 and B300.
Architecture-specific configurations preserve the centered FP32 backward
calculation, separate unscaled row maxima and logarithmic normalization,
and late gradient scaling. B200 and B300 use fused probability/dS consumers
for 128-column backward tiles; B300 retains its hardware TMEM reductions.
Interior probability tiles omit per-element bounds checks; tails and causal
boundaries retain visibility checks with the same centered arithmetic.

Blackwell uses packed FP32 arithmetic, overlapped operand/statistic transfers,
and adjacent D512 gradient slices. BF16 D512 MHA on B300 at 512 tokens
and above uses a register-resident FP32 auxiliary with 256-wide gradient
accumulators and vectorized gradient staging.

SM120 backward shares score products across query column warps for
D256/D512, combines row corrections before publishing them, and stages KV
statistics for the selected dense D256 and causal D64 configurations.
Aligned D512 forward and backward use full-width tiles with shared score
producers and separate output consumers. Consumer GPU backward pairs QK/dP
producers and packs DS/P stores. SM86/SM89 use wider D512 operand copies;
Ada uses tuned D256 tiles and cache policy, while SM120 also tunes causal
D128 query sharing.

The producer/consumer architecture in blackwell_pipeline.py adapts KohakuFA's
sm100/fwd.py and sm100/bwd.py at revision
0c5ede6859307bedc0c6089523c16b1ca51b7da9:
https://github.com/KohakuBlueleaf/KohakuFA
