The CuTe port retains centered backward and single-owner gradient tiles.

Causal BF16 D256 GQA uses overlapping forward stages on Ada and independent
K/V staging with ordered softmax warpgroups on Hopper. Short D64 cross-attention
queries split across the key sequence on Ada/Hopper. Native build caches include
the C++ source hash so copied checkouts cannot retain stale dispatch code.
Batch/head products above 65,535 flatten onto grid-x for attention, mask
packing and backward output-delta preparation; smaller grids are unchanged.

GB10 (SM121) uses shared D512 score tiles and streamed-feature D256/D512
short-sequence forward kernels. Runtime length dispatch preserves compiled
cache reuse across short-sequence boundaries.

Boolean masks are classified on every invocation, including CUDA graph replay.
Native eager autograd and compiler-safe custom operators share allocation and
TVM FFI dispatch. Compiled host entries are cached by device, tensor metadata
and sequence-length configuration, bounded to 128 entries and released before
Python shutdown.

